Subject: squashfs: genfscon with dedicated type instead of fs_use_xattr

RAUC verity bundles are squashfs images built on the host and carry no
xattr table; with fs_use_xattr the kernel refuses to mount them
(EOPNOTSUPP, "SELinux: (dev dm-0, type squashfs) has no xattr support").
Bundle integrity is enforced by CMS signature verification before mount
and dm-verity during reads, so per-file labels add nothing here.
A dedicated type (not fs_t) keeps the bundle filesystem distinguishable:
only tactiq_rauc_t is granted mount/read on it.

Observed on Rock 5A, first RAUC install attempt, 2026-07-15.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [TactiQ distro-specific labeling decision]

---
--- a/policy/modules/kernel/filesystem.te
+++ b/policy/modules/kernel/filesystem.te
@@ -39,7 +39,10 @@
 fs_use_xattr jfs gen_context(system_u:object_r:fs_t,s0);
 fs_use_xattr lustre gen_context(system_u:object_r:fs_t,s0);
 fs_use_xattr overlay gen_context(system_u:object_r:fs_t,s0);
-fs_use_xattr squashfs gen_context(system_u:object_r:fs_t,s0);
+# TactiQ: RAUC verity bundles carry no xattrs; see patch header.
+type tactiq_squashfs_t;
+fs_type(tactiq_squashfs_t)
+genfscon squashfs / gen_context(system_u:object_r:tactiq_squashfs_t,s0)
 fs_use_xattr ubifs gen_context(system_u:object_r:fs_t,s0);
 fs_use_xattr virtiofs gen_context(system_u:object_r:fs_t,s0);
 fs_use_xattr xfs gen_context(system_u:object_r:fs_t,s0);
